Journey: Claim of <amount> is decided at the right authority level
Id: decide-by-authority
Tags: @backoffice @claims @regression @authority
Risk: 4
Requirements: ADJ-2, ADJ-4
Actors: adjuster as adjuster, senior as senior-adjuster
Description: Data-dependent branching: within the adjuster's limit the adjuster approves; above it the claim is referred and a senior adjuster approves. Over-limit approval attempts are refused.

Run code "steps/claims.steps.ts#seedClaim" with policyId="POL-H-100231", type="FIRE", amount="<amount>" as seeded
Set variable claimId to seeded.claimId
Set variable overLimit to number("<amount>") > number(ADJUSTER_LIMIT)

As adjuster:
  Open ${BACKOFFICE_URL}/claims/${claimId}
    Expect the page contains "Review claim ${claimId}"
  Select "<reason>" from the "Decision reason" dropdown
  If ${overLimit} then
    # The adjuster first tries to approve: the system must refuse, then the adjuster refers it
    Click the "Approve" button
      Expect the page contains "exceeds your limit"
    Select "Over my authority" from the "Decision reason" dropdown
    Click the "Refer to senior" button
      Expect the page contains "referred to a senior adjuster"
    Expect the page does not contain "Approve"
  Otherwise
    Click the "Approve" button
      Expect the page contains "Claim ${claimId} approved"
  End

If ${overLimit} then
  As senior:
    Open ${BACKOFFICE_URL}/queue?show=referred
      Expect the "Claims queue" table contains "${claimId}"
    Click the "Review" link in the row containing "${claimId}"
      Expect the page contains "Status Referred"
    Select "Covered in full" from the "Decision reason" dropdown
    Click the "Approve" button
      Expect the page contains "Claim ${claimId} approved"
End

Get the first row of query "SELECT status, decision_by, referred_to FROM claims WHERE id = '${claimId}'" on claims as decided
Expect ${decided.status} equals "APPROVED"
Expect ${decided.decision_by} equals "<expectedDecider>"
Run code "steps/claims.steps.ts#removeClaim" with claimId="${claimId}" as cleanup

Examples:
  | amount   | reason           | expectedDecider  |
  | 4200.00  | Covered in full  | dana.okafor      |
  | 10000.00 | Covered in full  | dana.okafor      |
  | 18750.00 | Covered in full  | victor.lindqvist |
